// Alert query (DIAAT-205, new; DIAAT-285 rules): live dictation sessions warned that no
// speech was captured in the alert window. Replaces the browser Sentry alert on
// "dictation.no_speech_warning" (the browser no longer reports to Sentry).
//
// Source (browser, OBS-4; transcribe-web lib/dictation-session.ts, relayed by
// transcribe-api's POST /api/telemetry): "dictation.no_speech_warning" - recording has
// run for dictation.elapsed_seconds with no captured speech (microphone muted or wrong
// device, or Speech returning nothing).
// Area: dictation only (DIAAT-205, decision 1). Relayed browser events carry no hmcts.area,
// so the area comes from the journey type's prefix ("dictation.session" -> "dictation").
// Every event of the "dictation.session" journey counts the session as active.
// Output: failures = distinct sessions warned (hmcts.journey.id); failed_pct = 100 *
// failures / active sessions (context only). No code dimension: the event has none.
// Suggested rule (provisional): measure failures, Total, GreaterThanOrEqual 5, window
// PT30M, frequency PT10M, severity 2, no dimensions. Higher than speech-unhealthy's 3:
// one user's microphone is often the cause, so only several sessions at once point to
// a service (Speech) problem.
customEvents
| where tostring(customDimensions["hmcts.journey.type"]) == "dictation.session"
| extend area = coalesce(tostring(customDimensions["hmcts.area"]),
    tostring(split(tostring(customDimensions["hmcts.journey.type"]), ".")[0]))
| where area == "dictation"
| extend journey_id = tostring(customDimensions["hmcts.journey.id"])
| summarize sessions = dcount(journey_id),
    failures = dcountif(journey_id, name == "dictation.no_speech_warning")
| extend failed_pct = round(100.0 * failures / sessions, 1)
| project failures, failed_pct
